{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/1508226-lfg-v20-or-dav20-game-to-play-an-ancilla-elder-character-in","id":1508226,"title":"LFG V20 or DAV20 game to play an Ancilla/Elder character in","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-12T18:33:57-07:00","id":1508226,"title":"LFG V20 or DAV20 game to play an Ancilla/Elder character in","content":"I'm looking for a voice (also video if everyone is comfortable) V20 or DAV20 game. Either works or even the mix of them.<br /> <br /> <b>Character Concept:</b> Since I already played a lot of fledgling/neonate characters, I want to try to play an ancilla/elder character for a change. Unfortunately not a lot of games are created around old kindred players nor high level gameplay but I have a character concept that I want to play for a long time that its themes and vibes are mostly borrowed from John Milton's Paradise Lost and other media that portrays Lucifer as a tragic character. The character is a rebellious androgynous French noble Toreador who is mostly interested in painting, dancing and drinking in taverns instead of ruling or succeeding his father. He fell in love with a bard one day and ran away with her but quickly found himself to be groomed by the New Trinity that is following the The Dream of Michael.<br /> <br /> <b>Experience:</b> In WoD I have experience with Vampire: The Masquerade 5th and 20th edition, Demon: The Fallen and a little bit of Mage: The Ascension 20th also in video games I played Bloodlines, both Coteries and Shadows of New York and Heart of the Forest. I played a long running V5 chronicle and relatively long Demon chronicle. I wouldn't say I'm highly versed in lore that I know pretty much all the named characters and events but I have an overall knowledge about the universe that I can use in my character creation and roleplay fairly easily. Also In general I played Alien RPG, Cyberpunk RED, Pathfinder 2e and Dungeon Crawl Classics<br /> <br /> <b>Timezone:</b> I'm GMT+3 but if it's not so early or late for my timezone it does not matter that much.<br /> <br /> I was looking to play this character in chronicle that is modern times which he will be awoken in his really long torpor recently but I'm also down with full on Dark Ages game. It would probably be better to play this in an experienced ST's chronicle but I'm not that picky if you're new and in fact I would help as best as I can with everything I know. If this character concept sounds interesting to you and if you're running or planning run a game that is similar in vibes I would love to join your chronicle.<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27895-majordeckard","name":"MajorDeckard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27895_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}